                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.3332/91: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-07T16:00:00-03:00">June 7, 1940—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>253. For the Under Secretary. Department’s 156, June 6, 5 p.m. I agree that the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Wichita</hi> should arrive 3 days after the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Quincy</hi> is due to leave. However it should be made
                    very clear that the visit is entirely informal and that no entertaining of any
                    kind is expected.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
